# Dezco party reference must stay current

Whenever Dezco Knoleburn lore changes in this repo, update the quick party reference in the same turn:

`character/lore/dezco-party-reference.md`

## What counts as a change

Update the sheet if you add or edit any of:

1. Dezco’s identity, stats, colors, titles, mission, or personality
2. Family, Alzenhiem, names, crests, sigils
3. Yua, the King’s Lion, Rilock, the rival, timeline events
4. Secrets, what party members may know, or reveal timing
5. New play-session facts meant for party conversation
6. New journal entries, inventory, places, or travel status
7. Yua story plots, reveals, or magic systems (Mana Well, red/black meaning, etc.)

## Yua story plots

Longer Yua side plots live under `character/lore/yua-story-plots/`.

1. Keep future Yua reveals in that folder until a journal entry catches up
2. Still mirror any player facing facts onto the party reference sheet
3. Mark unrevealed material under **Secrets / do not spoil yet**

## Journal entries

Dezco’s journal lives as sequential files under `character/lore/journal/`:

1. Use the next number: `03-short-title.md`, then `04-...`, and so on
2. Do not dump new entries into one giant journal file
3. Update `character/lore/journal/README.md` when adding an entry
4. Keep the stub index at `character/lore/dezco-knoleburn-journal.md` in sync if needed

## How to update the party sheet

1. Put the new fact in the matching quick section (tables preferred).
2. Bump **Last updated** at the top of the sheet.
3. If it is a new in-play discovery, also add a row under **Blank lines for new party facts**.
4. Keep entries short and scannable. Long prose belongs in the other lore files; this sheet is for short-term memory friendly lookup while talking to party members.
5. Mark secrets clearly under **Secrets / do not spoil yet** when Dezco himself does not know them yet.

## Downloadable Google export

When lore/journal/Yua/crest content changes in a meaningful way, regenerate the Google Drive export pack in the same turn:

```bash
python3 character/lore/exports/build_dezco_lore_export.py
```

Outputs:
1. `character/lore/exports/Dezco_Knoleburn_Lore_Tabs.xlsx` (tabbed Google Sheets upload)
2. `character/lore/exports/Dezco_Knoleburn_Lore.docx` (Google Docs upload)

Commit the rebuilt files with the lore change.

## Do not skip

Even small lore tweaks must land on the party reference sheet. The sheet exists because the player relies on it for short-term memory support.
